  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Biodiversidad</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership for Sustainability Managed Fisheries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID South America Regional):  .The eastern Pacific is among the world&apos;s richest fisheries. The ecological impact of distant water fleets brings increased international attention to the challenges of illegal, unreported, and unregulated (IUU) fishing and the operations of these fleets frequently associated with corruption. Addressing IUU is critical for both biodiversity protection and livelihoods and food security of coastal communities. ..The partnership between NOAA and USAID aims to improve law enforcement capabilities in Ecuador, Peru and Colombia, improving the coordination on IUU and overfishing across the region. Under Component 1, NOAA will support regulators to identify and fight against IUU fishing and to advance implementation of the Port States Measurement Agreement (PSMA). Component 2 aims to improve management of fisheries and marine protected areas. This activity supports the Maritime SAFE Act (2019) and complements the efforts of the Mission to address climate change in marine ecosystems and promote biodiversity conservation of marine flora and fauna...With FY 2022 funding, NOAA will continue building the capacity of port inspectors to detect illegal fish catches, and strengthen the political will to implement Port States Measure Agreements (PSMA), via workshops, training, and ad hoc coaching. NOAA also plans to ramp up interventions  in support of the governments of Colombia and Ecuador to manage and enforce new restrictions around the Eastern Tropical Pacific Marine Corridor, a planned marine protected area with extremely high biodiversity, currently under threat from overfishing and other commercial activities. Peru will also benefit from  these set of interventions as observers, to improve their management of marine protected areas within their waters. Finally, the program will work with the governments of Peru and Ecuador to strengthen international agreements to manage deep-water fisheries. .. .</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Conservar la biodiversidad y gestionar los recursos naturales de manera que mantengan su viabilidad a largo plazo y preserven su potencial para satisfacer las necesidades de las generaciones presentes y futuras. Las actividades incluyen la lucha contra la explotaci&#xf3;n ilegal y corrupta de los recursos naturales y el control de especies invasoras. Los programas en este elemento deben integrarse con el &#xc1;rea de Agricultura bajo el &#xc1;rea de Crecimiento Econ&#xf3;mico y Mitigaci&#xf3;n de Conflictos y Reconciliaci&#xf3;n bajo la Categor&#xed;a de Paz y Seguridad, cuando sea aplicable y apropiado.</narrative>
  </description>
